    "q-163587": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163587",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis. When the displacement of $P$ from the origin is $x\\,m,$ the velocity is $v\\,m/s,$ and the acceleration is $(2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,{m/s}^{2}.$ If $P$ has velocity $1\\,m/s$ when its displacement is $1\\,m,$ find the values of $x$ for which $P$ is instantaneously at rest.",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14273713/assets/6046ef89f9abcc78be695d69df64471fb9c68645473c946e7f3212be27e2c6fb.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $(2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=2x-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}),\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=2x-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x=\\int (2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=1\\,m/s$ when $x=1\\,m,$ we can find the value of the constant $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2} & =(1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, the particle is instantaneously at rest when $v(x)=0\\,m/s.$ We find the displacement of the particle when instantaneously at rest by substituting $v=0$ in the equation above and solving for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2} & ={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ {x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x & =0 \\\\ x(x-\\frac{1}{2}) & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\,m,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
